# Environment for trip-packer.service
#
# Install as /opt/trip-packer/.env and reference from the unit if needed.
# Only two variables are read by the app; both have safe defaults, so this file
# is optional. It exists to make the deploy explicit rather than implicit.

NODE_ENV=production

# The listen port is NOT set here. It is the -p argument in ExecStart in
# trip-packer.service. Listing a PORT variable here would be misleading: the app
# never reads process.env.PORT, so editing it would silently do nothing.

# Absolute path to the SQLite database. Defaults to <cwd>/data/trip-packer.db,
# which resolves correctly under /opt/trip-packer. Set it explicitly anyway so
# the location does not silently depend on WorkingDirectory.
TRIP_PACKER_DB=/opt/trip-packer/data/trip-packer.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is deliberately NO secret here.
#
# Sessions are opaque random tokens stored in the `sessions` table and handed to
# the browser as an HttpOnly cookie. Nothing is signed with a server-side key,
# so there is no SESSION_SECRET to generate and no risk of leaking one by
# committing this file. Passwords are hashed with PBKDF2 and a per-user salt.
#
# If that ever changes, add the secret HERE and keep this file at mode 600 —
# do not put it in the systemd unit, where it would be visible to any user via
# `systemctl show`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
